<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>04 · BENCHMARKS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Three benchmarks, each owning one hypothesis
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Table
        style={{ width: 1160, height: 172, marginTop: 22 }}
        defaultTextStyle={{ fontSize: 14, textAlign: 'left', color: '#C3D0E2' }}
        defaultCellStyle={{ border: { bottom: { width: 1, color: '#1D2A40' } }, background: { color: '#0E1728' } }}
        cells={[
            [
                { text: 'Benchmark', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 13 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                { text: 'Tasks used here', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 13 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                { text: 'Protocol', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 13 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                { text: 'Owns', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 13 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
            ],
            [
                { text: 'PolyBench', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#4D8DFF' } },
                '6 main-table tasks: Tg, Tm, modulus, permeability, dielectric loss, IWLT',
                'Fixed 70/30 split × 3 model seeds',
                { text: 'H1', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF' } },
            ],
            ['PolyBench26', '2 tasks (PolyMetriX Tg, homopolymer density) + official architecture transfer', 'Official 5-fold, seed 42',
                { text: 'H2, H1-arch', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF' } }],
            ['OpenPoly', '3 properties: Tg, Tm, dielectric constant', 'Own 5-fold × 3 seeds × 5 n-levels (30 / 60 / 120 / 240 / all)',
                { text: 'H3, H4', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF' } }],
        ]}
    />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 44, marginTop: 24 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 470, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>POLYBENCH'S OWN THREE TIERS</Text>
            <Table
                style={{ width: 470, height: 132, marginTop: 10 }}
                defaultTextStyle={{ fontSize: 13, textAlign: 'left', color: '#C3D0E2' }}
                defaultCellStyle={{ border: { bottom: { width: 1, color: '#1D2A40' } }, background: { color: '#0E1728' } }}
                cells={[
                    ['tier', 'tasks', 'labelled rows'],
                    ['1', 'Tg, Tm', '8,055 / 3,796'],
                    ['2', 'modulus, permeability', '1,034 / 711'],
                    ['3', 'dielectric loss, IWLT', '279 / 228'],
                ]}
            />
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', justifyContent: 'center', gap: 14 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                Tier and sample size run in opposite directions: ρ(tier, log10 n) = −0.956.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.65 }}>
                So a tier label proxies two things at once — "needs chain information" and "has 30× less data". That conflation is
                announced here, on the slide where the tiers are introduced, not discovered later in the discussion.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#7E93AE', lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                Rule R1: one hypothesis is adjudicated inside one benchmark only. Numbers from different rows are never compared.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>5 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
